SUMMARY:Goosebumps The Musical: Phantom of the Auditorium
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261030
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261116
UID:1b186e257175d824c4d026ede2d1ac36@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Constellation Stage & Screen presents “Goosebumps The Musica
 l: Phantom of the Auditorium ” on stage October 30th- November 15th at t
 he Waldron Auditorium.\nGet ready for a frightfully fun adventure with Goo
 sebumps The Musical\, based on the wildly popular books by R. L. Stine! Wh
 en Brooke and Zeke are cast in their school’s spooky new play\, The Phan
 tom\, they start to wonder if the show is actually cursed. As strange mess
 ages appear and rehearsals are disrupted by a mysterious masked figure\, t
 hey must uncover the truth: is it all an elaborate prank… or is their th
 eater truly haunted? Full of catchy songs\, laugh-out-loud moments\, and j
 ust the right amount of Halloween-season chills\, this musical mystery is 
 perfect for kids\, tweens\, and grown-ups who remember reading by flashlig
 ht. Fun for all ages! \nSee Constellation’s website for more information
 \, including a detailed performance schedule. Learn more and find tickets 
 at https://seeconstellation.org/kids/goosebumps/
GEO:39.1657967;-86.5339376
LOCATION:Waldron Arts Center\, 122 S. Walnut St\, Bloomington\, IN 47403
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/goosebumps-the-musical-phantom-
 of-the-auditorium/58935/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learning Lab
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260616T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261218T160000
UID:a208e54198c96b67f1f5e9b7c441d383@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Explore 450 million years of Hoosier history. The IGWS Learnin
 g Lab is an experiential learning center that brings our collections out o
 f storage for hands-on discovery.\n Part museum\, part lab\, and part clas
 sroom\, the Learning Lab is where you can compare thousands of rocks\, min
 erals\, and fossils\, create art inspired by our collections\, explore rea
 l-time datasets\, and participate in interactive activities. Pull open dra
 wers to discover real specimens and question the world beneath your feet u
 sing scientific evidence.\n The Learning Lab is open to people of all ages
  and abilities from 10:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. Tuesday-Friday and 10:00 a.m. 
 to 5:00 p.m. on the third Saturday of the month. Parking is free! More inf
 ormation is available at https://igws.iu.edu/learninglab .
GEO:39.1719663;-86.5221333
LOCATION:Indiana Geological and Water Survey\, 5001 N. State Road 37 Busin
 ess\, Bloomington\, IN 47404
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/learning-lab/58810/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
