BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:City of Bloomington Halloween Trick or Treat
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261031T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261031T203000
UID:be61097fc9b8b735d2ce08bb27ce1099@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:City of Bloomington trick-or-treat hours have been set for Oct
 ober 31 from 5:30 - 8:30 p.m.\, RAIN or SHINE. \n Please consider these Ha
 lloween tips to help keep children and families safe:\n •Trick-or-treat 
 during designated hours and only go to those homes that have a porch light
  on to welcome trick-or-treaters.\n •Carry a flashlight to light the way
  on streets and sidewalks. A flashlight or glow sticks will also help illu
 minate children for motor vehicles.\n •Dress your children in\, or bring
  along\, some type of reflective material for dusk and later trick-or-trea
 ting. A reflective jacket works well\, as do reflecting trick-or-treat bag
 s. Sunset will be at 6:46 p.m. on Halloween.\n •Cross the street at corn
 ers\, using traffic signals and crosswalks.\n ªPut electronic devices suc
 h as cell phones down\, keep heads up and walk\, don't run.\n •Children 
 under the age of 12 should not be alone at night without adult supervision
 . If children are mature enough to be out without supervision\, they shoul
 d stick to familiar areas that are well-lit and trick-or-treat in groups.
 \n •Make sure that costumes do not cause a safety hazard for children by
  being too long or including masks that affect their ability to see clearl
 y. Choose face paint and makeup whenever possible instead of masks.\n •H
 omeowners should make sure that pets are secured so they do not become fri
 ghtened by costumed children or activity that is out of the ordinary.\n 
 •Children should be instructed to NEVER enter the home of someone they d
 o not know and to remain on the porch to receive their treats.\n •Any ob
 served suspicious activity or tainted candy should be reported to police i
 mmediately.\n •Children should be instructed to not eat candy until it h
 as been inspected by an adult.\n •Drive slowly\, anticipate pedestrian t
 raffic and turn your headlights on earlier in the day to spot children fro
 m greater distances.\n •Slow down and be especially alert in residential
  areas. Children are excited on Halloween and may move in unpredictable wa
 ys.\n •Take extra time to look for children at intersections\, on median
 s and on curbs and behind landscaping.
GEO:39.165325;-86.5263857
LOCATION:Bloomington\, IN
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/city-of-bloomington-halloween-t
 rick-or-treat/59964/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
