BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Two Tales of Terror: J-Horror Unleashed with Best Wishes to All/Mi
 na Ni Ko Are + Gozu
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261031T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261031T223000
UID:93fd4c4a52e5bc682b80ca52d1e4ae0a@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Snacks\, drinks in resealable/enclosed containers (there are n
 o cupholders in the Cinema!)\, and finger foods that do not emit a strong 
 odor or make a mess are allowed for this double feature. Alcohol\, cigaret
 tes\, electronic cigarettes\, and illicit drugs are prohibited at IU Cinem
 a.\nAbout Two Tales of Terror: J-Horror Unleashed with Best Wishes to All/
 Mina ni ko are + Gozu\nBest Wishes to All/Mina ni ko are (Yûta Shimotsu\,
  Japan\, 2023): A young woman's visit to her grandparents' home leads to t
 he discovery of what's brought them happiness\, a revelation that will lea
 d her to question her choices\, sanity\, and reality itself. [89 min\; hor
 ror\; Japanese with English subtitles]\nGozu (Takashi Miike\, Japan\, 2003
 ): Acclaimed director Takashi Miike's unhinged Yakuza/horror film continue
 s to shock and amaze audiences decades after its original release. Minami 
 is sent to kill his mentor Ozaki (who is in the midst of a nervous breakdo
 wn) but soon finds the simple hit quickly morphs into a terrifying and vis
 ceral journey into the unexplained and unknown. One of the films in Miike'
 s oeuvre that continues to confound and haunt audiences\, which is saying 
 something! [129 min\; horror\; Japanese with English subtitles]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/two-tales-of-terror-j-horror-un
 leashed-with-best-wishes-to-allmina-ni-ko-are-gozu/59871/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bloomington Community Farmers' Market
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261031T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261031T123000
UID:dc357713fae2db938f835a1a9a9eb144@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:The Bloomington Community Farmers' Market takes place rain or 
 shine every Saturday\, April through October\, at Showers Common next to C
 ity Hall\, 401 N. Morton St. in Bloomington.\n April-September: 8 a.m.-12:
 30 p.m.\nOctober: 9 a.m.-12:30 p.m.\n November: 9 a.m.-12:30 p.m. at the P
 avilion at Switchyard Park \n Nestled in picturesque downtown charm\, the 
 Bloomington Community Farmers' Market is a vital part of the local food cu
 lture. \n Market goers can expect to find a wide assortment of goods from
  the farm and field\, including fruits and vegetables\, eggs\, meats and c
 heeses\, honey\, seasonal flowers\, and annual and perennial plants. Food 
 and beverage artisans provide a tasteful variety of satisfying breads\, dr
 inks\, pastries\, and savory dishes. This weekly gathering provides indivi
 duals the opportunity to connect with their community in meaningful ways w
 hile supporting small farmers and businesses.
GEO:39.1496733;-86.5388079
LOCATION:Showers Common\, 402 N Morton Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47404
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/bloomington-community-farmers-m
 arket/57685/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
