DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261101T214500
UID:dd66ee5754a3668b9a3d3d7a6b580eb9@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:After years of consolidating his empire\, the elderly Great Lo
 rd Hidetora Ichimonji decides to abdicate and divide his domain amongst hi
 s three sons. The eldest\, Taro\, will rule\, and his second and third son
 s—Jiro and Saburo—will take command of his second and third castles\, 
 but are expected to obey their eldest brother. When Sabura is banished for
  disobedience\, the (literal) Shakespearean dramatics play out in Kurosawa
 ’s third adaptation of the Bard. Widely considered one of the greatest f
 ilms ever made and among Kurosawa’s finest filmmaking achievements\, Ran
  continues to set the bar in formally inventive and meticulously crafted a
 daptive storytelling. [160 min\; tragedy\, drama\, war\; Japanese with Eng
 lish subtitles]
GEO:39.168585;-86.517361
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. 7th Street\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
