BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Photographic Reflex: The Lee Marks and John C. DePrez Jr. Coll
 ection
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261107
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261108
UID:81641b24d3b7aeda897434f7098256c1@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Spanning more than 150 years\, The Photographic Reflex celebra
 tes a transformative gift to the Eskenazi Museum of Art at Indiana Univers
 ity: more than one hundred works by eighty artists\, generously donated by
  Lee Marks and John C. DePrez Jr. This exhibition features photographs dat
 ing from 1856 to 2017 and highlights the medium’s extraordinary range\, 
 both as a tool for documentation and as a vehicle for artistic exploration
 .\nFrom Alfred Stieglitz’s delicate studies of grass to Richard Misrach
 ’s vast images of the cosmos\, photographers have long found inspiration
  in the natural world. The built environment has also served as a compelli
 ng subject\, and the exhibition includes Berenice Abbott’s striking view
 s of 1920s New York City as well as Edward Burtynsky’s sweeping industri
 al landscapes.\nPhotography has played a central role in witnessing confli
 ct\, from Timothy H. O’Sullivan’s Civil War battlefield to iconic imag
 es from World War II\, Vietnam\, and beyond. While often associated with s
 traightforward depictions of reality\, photography also allows artists to 
 experiment with light\, exposure\, and process to construct imaginative sc
 enes and images beyond human sight.\nThe Photographic Reflex: The Lee Mark
 s and John C. DePrez Jr. Collection reveals photography’s power to refle
 ct and shape our perception of the world around us across time\, space\, a
 nd vision.\nLead support for this exhibition has been generously provided 
 by the Martha and David Moore Prints\, Drawings and Photographs Endowment
 \; Peter and Pamela DePrez\; Anne Marks Morgan\; Gregory Morse\; Efroymson
  Family Fund\; Anne N. DePrez\; John J. Medveckis\; and Friends of Lee Mar
 ks and John DePrez Jr.\nAdditional support provided by John M. (Jack) Reyn
 olds\, Jeffrey A. Wolin\, Sandi Clark\, and Katherine Campbell and Robert 
 J. Boeglin Jr.\, M.D.
GEO:39.1688819;-86.5198163
LOCATION:Eskenazi Museum of Art at Indiana University\, 1133 E. 7th Street
 \, Fine Arts Plaza\, Bloomington\, IN 47405
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/the-photographic-reflex-the-lee
 -marks-and-john-c-deprez-jr-collection/60101/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hotel California &#8211\; The Original Eagles Tribute
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261108T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261108T213000
UID:c500134da39635023da10def55d5db2f@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:For over three decades now HOTEL CALIFORNIA have been recreati
 ng the legendary sound of The Eagles\, and thrilling audiences all over th
 e world. From the quintessential Eagles anthem “Hotel California” thru
  “Take It Easy”\, “Lyin’ Eyes”\, “Take It to the Limit”\, 
 “Peaceful Easy Feeling”\, “One of These Nights”\, “Dirty Laundry
 ”\, “Already Gone”\, “The Long Run”\, “Life In the Fast Lane
 ” and “Desperado”\, they have evolved into a masterful celebration o
 f The Eagles’ music.\nThe band set the bar in 1986\, and they’ve remai
 ned the industry leading substitute for The Eagles ever since. Playing to 
 huge outdoor and arena audiences\, sharing bills with some of rock’s leg
 ends\, and going places no tribute band has gone before. A long run by any
  measure\, but it begs the question – what makes HOTEL CALIFORNIA so spe
 cial?\nSimply put\, incredible lead vocal similarity\, intensely accurate 
 instrumental work\, soaring harmonies\, and top-flight live performances\,
  just for starters. These are the band’s hallmarks\, and the foundation 
 on which their reputation has been built. With over a century of collectiv
 e professional experience in the band today\, they’re still going strong
 er than ever!\nIf you love The Eagles\, then welcome to the HOTEL CALIFORN
 IA – you’ve just found the next-best thing.
GEO:39.1662844;-86.5328085
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/hotel-california-8211-the-origi
 nal-eagles-tribute/58776/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Interfaith Thanksgiving Community Concert and Food Drive
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261108T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261108T193000
UID:d195e27f1e4ee98205633869c411f533@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:Interfaith Community Concert and Food Drive\nJoin us for a spe
 cial evening of music\, gratitude\, and fellowship as several faith commun
 ities come together to share music and meaningful expressions of their tra
 ditions. This free community event is open to everyone\, and all are warml
 y welcome!\nThrough music\, prayer\, and expressions of faith\, we’ll ha
 ve the opportunity to worship together\, learn from one another\, and cele
 brate the things that unite us. Whether you come to enjoy the music\, refl
 ect on what you’re grateful for\, or connect with your neighbors\, we in
 vite you to be part of this special gathering!\nWe’ll also put gratitude
  into action by supporting Hoosier Hills Food Bank’s holiday food drive.
  Please consider bringing needed holiday food items to help local families
  in need this season.\nInvite a friend\, bring your family\, and join us f
 or an evening of music\, gratitude\, and connection! Together\, we can bui
 ld bridges of understanding\, strengthen our community\, and share the spi
 rit of giving.\nEveryone. Every Tradition. One Community.\nSunday\, Novemb
 er 8\, 2026 | 6:00–7:30 p.m.\nUnitarian Universalist Church of Bloomingt
 on\n2120 N. Fee Lane\, Bloomington\, Indiana\nAdmission is free. Stay afte
 rward for refreshments and fellowship. We look forward to welcoming you!
GEO:39.185303;-86.51871709999999
LOCATION:Unitarian Universalist Church\, 2120 N Fee Ln.\, Bloomington\, IN
  47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/interfaith-thanksgiving-communi
 ty-concert-and-food-drive/60136/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
END:VEVENT
