BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tokyo Godfathers (2003)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261206T200000
UID:0eef58c83face99a8514f36cc09901c8@visitbloomington.com
DESCRIPTION:For those who love the BCT’s Studio Ghibli series!\nTokyo Go
 dfathers is a 2003 Japanese animated Christmas tragicomedy adventure film 
 written and directed by Satoshi Kon.\nOne Christmas Eve\, three homeless p
 eople—middle-aged alcoholic Gin\, transgender woman Hana\, and teenage r
 unaway Miyuki—discover an abandoned newborn while searching through the 
 garbage\, along with a note asking whoever finds the baby to take good car
 e of her and a key leading to a locker containing a bag holding clues to t
 he parents’ identity. The trio sets out to find the baby’s parents\, a
 nd Hana names her Kiyoko\, after the Japanese title of “Silent Night\,
 ” meaning “pure child”.\nRated: PG-13\nLength: 1hr 32mins\nFormat: D
 CP
GEO:39.1662844;-86.5328085
LOCATION:Buskirk-Chumley Theater\, 114 E. Kirkwood Avenue\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47408
URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/event/tokyo-godfathers-2003/60157/
X-SOURCE:Visit Bloomington
X-SOURCE-URL:https://www.visitbloomington.com/events/
